IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (Western Australia), with the Security and Related Activities
-- (Control) Regulations 1997 -- who is a security officer and what licence the work needs (ss 3, 4, 11-14A, 28, 35); who
-- need not hold one (s 5, regs 5A, 5B, s 42A(3)); the offence of working unlicensed and the employment rules around it
-- (ss 15, 16, 19, 20, 43); firearms and batons (ss 23-26, reg 9, Sch 1 cl 9, 11); when a person is a prohibited person
-- (ss 4A, 4B, regs 24, 25, Sch 2), including how a spent or youth matter counts; whether a licence may be issued
-- (ss 46, 47, 52, 52A, 53, regs 16, 17); how long it runs and how it is renewed (ss 42A, 49, 55, 57, 60); the fees
-- (reg 54, Sch 4); what a licensed officer must do at work and afterwards (ss 61, 77, 77A, Sch 1 cl 7, 11B); what can
-- happen to the licence (ss 67A, 79B, 80, 81); review (s 72); and the fines (Sch 5 modified penalties).
--
-- SEAT: the security officer and licence applicant (Jake, at 27, joining Sentinel Security Services Pty Ltd). Every
-- decision is phrased as that person would ask it: "Am I a security officer?", "May I do this work without a security
-- officer's licence?", "Am I a prohibited person?", "Can I be issued a security officer's licence?", "How long will my
-- licence run?", "Is my renewal application on time?". Where the Act hands a judgment to the licensing officer or the
-- Commissioner (s 52(1)(c) "good character ... fit and proper", (cb) "extenuating circumstances", (e), (k), s 52A(2)
-- "contrary to the public interest", s 53 exemption, s 49(3) "such later time as the licensing officer ... allows",
-- s 55(2)(b) "appropriate", s 67A "of the opinion", "satisfied"), the answer is conditional on that judgment, which is
-- asked as a fact.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 3 ("disqualifying offence", "licence", "remuneration", "supplies"), s 4, s 4A, s 4B, s 5,
-- s 11, s 12, s 13(a), s 14(1), (2), s 14A, s 15, s 16, s 19, s 20, s 23, s 24(1), s 25(1), (1a), (2), s 26(1)-(3),
-- s 28(1), s 35(1), s 42A, s 43, s 46(1), s 47(1)(f), s 49(3), s 52(1), s 52A(2), s 53, s 55, s 57, s 60, s 61(2),
-- s 64, s 67A(1), (2), s 69(1a), s 72, s 77(2), s 77A(1), s 79B, s 80(1), s 81(1), s 88A(1), (5);
-- regs 5A, 5B, 9, 16(1)(a), (b), (1A), 17(1)(f), 24, 25, 54; Sch 1 cl 7, 9, 11(2), 11B; Sch 2 (the Division 1 and
-- Division 2 headings, as an input); Sch 4 (the fees for licences other than agent's licences); Sch 5 Div 1 items 2, 21,
-- 24, 27, 28.
--
-- Edition: the Act as compiled on legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 48361, retrieved 7 September 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_48361.txt; its latest amendments shown are the Firearms Act 2024 (No. 23 of 2024)
-- ss 485-487 and the Criminal Law (Mental Impairment) Act 2023 (No. 10 of 2023). The Regulations as deposited at
-- ../../../security-and-related-activities-control-regulations-1997/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49704.txt (version
-- 07-ae0-00, currency from 1 July 2026, retrieved 20 October 2026); Schedule 4 as inserted by SL 2026/115 r. 11.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: Part 2 (administration, secrecy, the register); Parts 4 and 5 beyond the definitions (inquiry and crowd
-- control licensing, which run parallel to Part 3); Part 6 (armed bodyguards); s 42B and agent's licences beyond whether
-- one is needed; s 44, s 45, s 56 (licences held for partnerships and companies); s 47(2b)-(4), s 48 (fingerprints, apart
-- from the fee), s 50, s 68A; the classes of consultant's and installer's licence (regs 26, 27); Division 4 of Part 7
-- beyond what may happen to the licence (the State Administrative Tribunal's disciplinary powers in s 67 are named, not
-- worked out); s 69 beyond (1a); records (ss 78, 84-87); drug testing procedure (Part 7 of the Regulations); the Firearms
-- Act 2024, which s 24(4) adds on top; the Schedule 2 offence list itself (which Division an offence falls in is an INPUT);
-- and the Spent Convictions Act 1988 and Young Offenders Act 1994, which decide whether a matter is spent.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA)`

§§ `numbers and helpers`

-- s 52(1)(b): "the applicant has attained the age of 18 years".
`the minimum age for a security officer's licence` MEANS 18

-- s 4A(2): "a finding of guilt made on, or after, 1 January 1996".
`the first day a finding of guilt counts` MEANS Date 1 1 1996

-- reg 25(2)(a), (b): "10 years" and "5 years" from the date of the finding of guilt.
`the long disqualifying period in years` MEANS 10
`the short disqualifying period in years` MEANS 5

-- reg 25(3)(b): "no penalty, or a penalty of, or in total of, less than $500".
`the Division 2 penalty threshold` MEANS 500

-- s 49(3): "no later than 28 days before the day on which the licence is due to expire".
`the days before expiry to apply for renewal` MEANS 28

-- s 57(2): notice of a refused renewal "no later than 14 days before the day on which the licence is due to expire".
`the days before expiry for notice of a refused renewal` MEANS 14

-- s 57(1): notice of a refused issue "no later than 28 days after the decision is made".
`the days after a refused issue for notice` MEANS 28

-- s 77A(1): "within 7 days"; s 77(2): "not later than 14 days after the change occurs".
`the days to report a charge or a finding of guilt` MEANS 7
`the days to report a new home address` MEANS 14

GIVEN `born on` IS A DATE
      `on`      IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`age in completed years` MEANS
    IF     DATE_MONTH `on` GREATER THAN DATE_MONTH `born on`
        OR (DATE_MONTH `on` EQUALS DATE_MONTH `born on` AND DATE_DAY `on` AT LEAST DATE_DAY `born on`)
    THEN DATE_YEAR `on` MINUS DATE_YEAR `born on`
    ELSE DATE_YEAR `on` MINUS DATE_YEAR `born on` MINUS 1

-- The same day and month, a number of years later. (A 29 February start is not handled; none arises here.)
GIVEN `d` IS A DATE
      `n` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`years after` MEANS Date (DATE_DAY `d`) (DATE_MONTH `d`) (DATE_YEAR `d` PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `earlier` IS A DATE
      `later`   IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from` MEANS Day `later` MINUS Day `earlier`

§§ `11-14A, 28, 35 -- what my work is`

-- The work, as the person doing it could describe it. Each limb is a definition in Part 3, 4 or 5 Division 1.
-- s 3: "remuneration includes any forbearance or other valuable consideration". s 93 presumes remuneration once it is
-- proved the person was engaged to do the thing.
DECLARE `My work` HAS
    `I am paid for it`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 3 "remuneration"
    `I watch, guard or protect property`                                        IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 12(1)
    `my one employer, not a security agent, employs me to guard its own property` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 12(2)
    `I carry a firearm or baton while working`                                  IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 12(2)
    `I escort a person as a guard or protector`                                 IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 14A
    `I advise on watching, guarding or protecting property`                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 13(a)
    `I install, maintain or repair security equipment listed in s 14`           IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 14(1), regs 6-8
    `the equipment is in a vehicle, vessel or aircraft`                         IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 14(2)
    `as a regular duty I control, screen or remove people at a venue or event`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 35(1)
    `I investigate people's conduct or character, or look for missing persons`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 28(1)
    `I supply other people to do security work`                                 IS A BOOLEAN  -- ss 11, 27, 34
    `I am on official duty as a police officer or in the Defence Force`         IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 5(1)
    `I am on official duty as a public officer`                                 IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 5(2), (3)
    `I am a court security, custodial or prison services contract worker doing that work` IS A BOOLEAN  -- regs 5A, 5B
    `I hold a temporary licence covering this work`                             IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 42A(3)

-- s 12(1): "A security officer is a person who for remuneration watches, guards or protects any property."
-- (2): "A person employed by one employer only, who is not a security agent, to watch, guard or protect the property of
-- that employer is not within the definition in subsection (1) unless the person is in possession of a firearm or baton
-- while carrying out his or her duties."
@export Am I a security officer (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 12)?
GIVEN `my work` IS A `My work` @desc The work you do or are about to do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a security officer` IF
        `my work`'s `I am paid for it`
    AND `my work`'s `I watch, guard or protect property`
    AND (    (NOT `my work`'s `my one employer, not a security agent, employs me to guard its own property`)
          OR `my work`'s `I carry a firearm or baton while working`)

-- The licences the Act creates (s 3). Agent's licences (s 3 "agent's licence") are one entry here.
DECLARE `Licence type` IS ONE OF
    `a security officer's licence`
    `a security bodyguard's licence`
    `a security consultant's licence`
    `a security installer's licence`
    `a crowd controller's licence`
    `an investigator's licence`
    `an agent's licence`

-- ss 15-18A, 29, 30, 36, 37: "A person must not act as a ... except under the authority of a ... licence." Each licence
-- answers one definition: s 13(a) consultant, s 14 installer (not equipment in a vehicle, vessel or aircraft: s 14(2)),
-- s 14A bodyguard ("for remuneration escorts another person as a guard or protector"), s 35 crowd controller, s 28
-- investigator, ss 11, 27, 34 agents ("supplies the services of"). One job can need more than one licence.
@export Does my work need this licence (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) Part 3, 4 or 5)?
GIVEN `the licence` IS A `Licence type` @desc The licence you are asking about
      `my work` IS A `My work` @desc The work you do or are about to do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my work need this licence` IF
    CONSIDER `the licence`
    WHEN `a security officer's licence` THEN `Am I a security officer` `my work`
    WHEN `a security bodyguard's licence` THEN `my work`'s `I am paid for it` AND `my work`'s `I escort a person as a guard or protector`
    WHEN `a security consultant's licence` THEN `my work`'s `I am paid for it` AND `my work`'s `I advise on watching, guarding or protecting property`
    WHEN `a security installer's licence` THEN `my work`'s `I am paid for it`
                                           AND `my work`'s `I install, maintain or repair security equipment listed in s 14`
                                           AND (NOT `my work`'s `the equipment is in a vehicle, vessel or aircraft`)
    WHEN `a crowd controller's licence` THEN `my work`'s `I am paid for it` AND `my work`'s `as a regular duty I control, screen or remove people at a venue or event`
    WHEN `an investigator's licence` THEN `my work`'s `I am paid for it` AND `my work`'s `I investigate people's conduct or character, or look for missing persons`
    WHEN `an agent's licence` THEN `my work`'s `I supply other people to do security work`

§§ `5, regs 5A, 5B, 42A -- who need not be licensed`

-- s 5(1): while performing official duties as a member of the Commonwealth Defence Forces or an officer of a police force,
-- "he or she is not required to comply with Parts 3, 4, 5 and 6." (2): a public officer on official duties "is not required
-- to comply with Part 3, other than Division 3, or with Parts 4 and 5." Regs 5A(2), 5B(2): court security, custodial and
-- prison services contract workers are "exempt from all of the provisions of the Act" for that work.
-- s 42A(3): "The holder of a temporary licence under this section does not commit an offence under this Act while acting
-- under and in accordance with that licence."
@export Am I excused from holding a licence for this work (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 5, s 42A; Regulations regs 5A, 5B)?
GIVEN `my work` IS A `My work` @desc The work you do or are about to do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I excused from holding a licence` IF
       `my work`'s `I am on official duty as a police officer or in the Defence Force`
    OR `my work`'s `I am on official duty as a public officer`
    OR `my work`'s `I am a court security, custodial or prison services contract worker doing that work`
    OR `my work`'s `I hold a temporary licence covering this work`

§§ `16, 15, 19, 20, 43 -- may I work unlicensed`

-- s 16: "A person must not act as a security officer except under the authority of a security officer's licence.
-- Penalty: a fine of $15 000."
@export May I do this work without a security officer's licence (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 16)?
GIVEN `my work` IS A `My work` @desc The work you do or are about to do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I do this work without a security officer's licence` IF
       (NOT `Am I a security officer` `my work`)
    OR `Am I excused from holding a licence` `my work`

-- s 19(1): "A person who is licensed as a -- (a) security officer ... must not act as such unless he or she does so as an
-- employee of a security agent." s 4: "references to employment are to employment under a contract of service or
-- apprenticeship." (2): not a licensed security agent acting under his own security officer's licence.
-- s 11: "A security agent is a person who supplies the services of -- (a) security officers". The test is the definition,
-- not the agent's licence: an unlicensed agent is still a security agent (its own breach is s 15, and s 20 for employing).
@export As a licensed security officer, may I work on these terms (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 19)?
GIVEN `I hold a security officer's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a security officer's licence
      `I am an employee, under a contract of service or apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you work under a contract of service or an apprenticeship, rather than as a contractor
      `the business I work for supplies the services of security officers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business you work for supplies security officers to others (a security agent)
      `I am myself a licensed security agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a security agent's licence yourself
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a licensed security officer, may I work on these terms` IF
        `I hold a security officer's licence`
    AND (    (`I am an employee, under a contract of service or apprenticeship` AND `the business I work for supplies the services of security officers`)
          OR `I am myself a licensed security agent`)

-- s 15: "A person must not act as a security agent except under the authority of a security agent's licence." s 11: a
-- security agent "supplies the services of -- (a) security officers". s 43(1): "A licence can only be issued to a natural
-- person"; (2): a natural person who is a director or officer may hold the agent's licence "on behalf of ... a body
-- corporate". So a company that places officers at a client's building needs a security agent's licence, held for it by
-- one of its officers. A business that guards only its own property with its own staff supplies no one's services.
@export Must the business I work for hold a security agent's licence (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) ss 11, 15, 43)?
GIVEN `the business supplies the services of security officers to others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business places security officers at clients' premises or otherwise supplies their services
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the business I work for hold a security agent's licence` IF
    `the business supplies the services of security officers to others`

-- s 20(1)(a): "A person must not employ as a -- (a) security officer a person who does not hold a security officer's
-- licence". From the officer's seat: no one may put me on the roster until my licence is issued.
@export May I be employed as a security officer before my licence is issued (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 20)?
GIVEN `I hold a security officer's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your security officer's licence has been issued
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be employed as a security officer` IF `I hold a security officer's licence`

§§ `23-26, reg 9, Sch 1 cl 9, 11 -- firearms and batons`

-- s 26(1): "a security officer's licence does not authorise the holder to be in possession of a baton". (2): only if "(a)
-- his or her licence is endorsed under subsection (3) ... and (b) the baton is of a type approved by the Commissioner by
-- order published in the Gazette." Sch 1 Div 2A cl 11(2): an officer with a s 26 endorsement "must successfully complete an
-- approved training course in baton use within the period of 12 months" after the last one (a condition: s 64).
@export May I carry a baton while working (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 26; Regulations Sch 1 cl 9(2), 11(2))?
GIVEN `my licence has a baton endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your security officer's licence is endorsed under s 26
      `the baton is a type the Commissioner approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the baton is of a type approved by Gazette order
      `my baton training is within the last 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you completed approved baton training within 12 months of the last course
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I carry a baton while working` IF
    `my licence has a baton endorsement` AND `the baton is a type the Commissioner approved` AND `my baton training is within the last 12 months`

-- s 24(1): a licence "may be endorsed ... to authorise the security officer to be in possession of a firearm while engaged
-- in ... (a) the escort of money or articles of value; (b) any other prescribed activity, but not otherwise." Reg 9: an ATM
-- or a safe malfunctioning or being repaired or serviced; money or valuables at a place of business specified in a security
-- agent's licence. s 25: a permit, only for an endorsed officer, "for a particular display or other special occasion".
-- s 23: without the endorsement (and compliance with it), possession is an offence. Sch 1 cl 9(1): only a firearm "provided
-- to the security officer by the security agent". The Firearms Act 2024 applies on top (s 24(4)); not encoded.
DECLARE `Armed task` IS ONE OF
    `escorting money or articles of value`
    `guarding an ATM or safe that is malfunctioning or being serviced`
    `guarding money or valuables at the business place named in the agent's licence`
    `guarding money or valuables at a special occasion`
    `ordinary guarding of a building`

@export May I carry a firearm for this task (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) ss 23-25; Regulations reg 9, Sch 1 cl 9(1))?
GIVEN `the task` IS A `Armed task` @desc What you would be doing while armed
      `my licence has a firearm endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your security officer's licence is endorsed under s 24
      `I hold a permit for this occasion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a s 25 permit for this display or special occasion
      `the security agent provided the firearm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the firearm was provided to you by the security agent you work for
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I carry a firearm for this task` IF
        `my licence has a firearm endorsement`
    AND `the security agent provided the firearm`
    AND (CONSIDER `the task`
         WHEN `guarding money or valuables at a special occasion` THEN `I hold a permit for this occasion`
         WHEN `ordinary guarding of a building` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

§§ `4A, 4B, regs 24, 25, Sch 2 -- am I a prohibited person`

-- s 4B(1): a finding of guilt is "(a) a court making a formal finding of guilt ...; (b) a court convicting the person ...,
-- if there has been no formal finding of guilt before conviction; (c) a court accepting a plea of guilty ...; (d) a finding
-- under The Criminal Code section 27 that the person is not guilty ... on account of mental impairment ...; (e) a finding
-- under the Criminal Law (Mental Impairment) Act 2023 section 41(2)(c)". Every limb is a court's act. A police caution or a
-- juvenile justice team referral (Young Offenders Act 1994 Part 5) is not a court's act, so (an inference) it is not one.
DECLARE `What happened to the charge` IS ONE OF
    `a court formally found me guilty`
    `a court convicted me`
    `a court accepted my plea of guilty`
    `a court found me not guilty on account of mental impairment`
    `a finding under the Criminal Law (Mental Impairment) Act 2023 s 41(2)(c)`
    `police cautioned me`
    `police referred me to a juvenile justice team`
    `a court acquitted me`
    `the charge is still pending`

-- reg 24: disqualifying offences are those "described in Schedule 2", and equivalents elsewhere. Sch 2 Division 1 includes
-- Criminal Code indictable offences with a maximum over 3 years' imprisonment (other than plain s 378), Misuse of Drugs Act
-- 1981 indictable offences, Firearms Act indictable offences and Commonwealth terrorism offences. Division 2 includes
-- Criminal Code s 378 stealing (other than a "special case"), ss 75, 172, 190, 191, 202, 313, 445, 474, 514, simple Misuse
-- of Drugs offences, and all Medicines and Poisons Act 2014 and Weapons Act 1999 offences. Which Division is an INPUT.
DECLARE `Schedule 2 place` IS ONE OF
    `a Division 1 offence`
    `a Division 2 offence`
    `not a disqualifying offence`

-- One charge and what came of it, as the person could describe it.
DECLARE `My past matter` HAS
    `what happened`                                         IS A `What happened to the charge`
    `the date of the outcome`                               IS A DATE
    `where the offence sits in Schedule 2`                  IS A `Schedule 2 place`
    `it was later quashed or set aside`                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 4B(2)(a)
    `a law lets me not disclose it`                         IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 4B(3): "spent"
    `it came from my first Division 2 incident`             IS A BOOLEAN  -- reg 25(3)(a)
    `the total penalty for Division 2 offences from that incident` IS A NUMBER  -- reg 25(3)(b)

@export Is this a finding of guilt under the Act (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 4B)?
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `My past matter` @desc A charge against you and what came of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this a finding of guilt` IF
        (NOT `the matter`'s `it was later quashed or set aside`)
    AND (CONSIDER `the matter`'s `what happened`
         WHEN `police cautioned me` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `police referred me to a juvenile justice team` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `a court acquitted me` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `the charge is still pending` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

-- The disqualifying period, in years, for a finding of guilt of a disqualifying offence; 0 where none is prescribed.
-- reg 25(2): "(a) in the case of a Division 1 offence, unless the finding of guilt in relation to the offence is a spent
-- conviction -- 10 years commencing on the date the finding of guilt was made; or (b) otherwise -- 5 years". (3): no period
-- for a Division 2 offence "if the offence arose from the first Division 2 incident involving the person; and ... no
-- penalty, or a penalty of, or in total of, less than $500 is imposed".
-- s 4B(2)(b): "a reference to a conviction includes a reference to a spent conviction", and (3) makes it spent "if, under a
-- law in any jurisdiction, the prohibited person is permitted not to disclose" it. So spent does not wipe a Division 1
-- matter out; it shortens the period from 10 years to 5. A youth conviction that the Young Offenders Act 1994 s 189 treats
-- as spent would take the 5 years (an inference; whether it is spent is asked).
@export How many years does this matter disqualify me for (Regulations reg 25)?
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `My past matter` @desc A charge against you and what came of it
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many years does this matter disqualify me for` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Is this a finding of guilt` `the matter`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `the matter`'s `where the offence sits in Schedule 2`
         WHEN `not a disqualifying offence` THEN 0
         WHEN `a Division 1 offence` THEN
             IF `the matter`'s `a law lets me not disclose it`
             THEN `the short disqualifying period in years`
             ELSE `the long disqualifying period in years`
         WHEN `a Division 2 offence` THEN
             IF     `the matter`'s `it came from my first Division 2 incident`
                AND `the matter`'s `the total penalty for Division 2 offences from that incident` LESS THAN `the Division 2 penalty threshold`
             THEN 0
             ELSE `the short disqualifying period in years`

-- s 4A(1): "a person is a prohibited person -- (a) if there has been a finding of guilt in relation to a disqualifying
-- offence committed by the person; and (b) during the disqualifying period prescribed in respect of the offence." (2): only
-- for "a finding of guilt made on, or after, 1 January 1996." The period runs "commencing on the date the finding of guilt
-- was made", so it ends the day before the anniversary.
@export Am I a prohibited person because of this matter on this day (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 4A; Regulations reg 25)?
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `My past matter` @desc A charge against you and what came of it
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is asked
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a prohibited person because of it` IF
        `How many years does this matter disqualify me for` `the matter` GREATER THAN 0
    AND Day (`the matter`'s `the date of the outcome`) AT LEAST Day `the first day a finding of guilt counts`
    AND Day `on` AT LEAST Day (`the matter`'s `the date of the outcome`)
    AND Day `on` LESS THAN Day (`years after` (`the matter`'s `the date of the outcome`) (`How many years does this matter disqualify me for` `the matter`))

-- A person with several matters is a prohibited person if any one of them makes them one.
@export Am I a prohibited person on this day (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 4A)?
GIVEN `my matters` IS A LIST OF `My past matter` @desc Every charge against you and what came of each
      `on` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is asked
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a prohibited person` IF
    any (GIVEN m YIELD `Am I a prohibited person because of it` m `on`) `my matters`

§§ `46, 47, 52, 52A, 53, regs 16, 17 -- can I be issued a licence`

-- An application for a security officer's licence (not a temporary licence), as the applicant could describe it. The
-- licensing officer's judgments are asked as facts.
DECLARE `My application` HAS
    `my date of birth`                                                    IS A DATE
    `the date of the decision`                                            IS A DATE
    `my past matters`                                                     IS A LIST OF `My past matter`
    `it is in the approved form, lodged as prescribed, with the fee`      IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 46(1), reg 14
    `the officer accepts the evidence of my identity`                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 52(1)(a), reg 18
    `the officer is satisfied I am of good character and fit and proper`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 52(1)(c), s 52A(1)
    `a charge for a disqualifying offence is pending against me`          IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 52(1)(cb)
    `the officer is satisfied extenuating circumstances exist`            IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 52(1)(cb)
    `the officer is satisfied I can comply with the licence conditions`   IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 52(1)(e)
    `I will do monitoring duties only`                                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- reg 16(1A)
    `I have completed the prescribed training course`                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 52(1)(g)(i), reg 16(1)(a), (b)
    `the officer exempted me from the training course`                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 53(2)
    `I have passed the written examination`                               IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 52(1)(g)(ii), reg 17(1)(f)
    `I am applying for a firearm endorsement`                             IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 24
    `I am applying for a baton endorsement`                               IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 26
    `I have passed the prescribed medical examination`                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 52(1)(h), reg 15
    `the officer is satisfied issuing it is not contrary to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 52A(2)
    `the officer sees no other good reason to refuse`                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 52(1)(k)

-- reg 16(1): the course for "(a) a security officer's licence with an endorsement under section 26, an approved training
-- course in watching, guarding and protecting property including the use of a baton; (b) any other security officer's
-- licence, an approved training course in watching, guarding and protecting property". (1A): these "do not apply ... to the
-- extent that the applicant ... will be undertaking monitoring duties only (e.g. ... in a security control room)".
DECLARE `Training course` IS ONE OF
    `none is prescribed: monitoring duties only`
    `watching, guarding and protecting property`
    `watching, guarding and protecting property, including the use of a baton`

@export Which training course must I complete for a security officer's licence (Regulations reg 16)?
GIVEN `the application` IS A `My application` @desc Your application for a security officer's licence
GIVETH A `Training course`
`Which training course must I complete` MEANS
    IF `the application`'s `I am applying for a baton endorsement`
    THEN `watching, guarding and protecting property, including the use of a baton`
    ELSE IF `the application`'s `I will do monitoring duties only`
         THEN `none is prescribed: monitoring duties only`
         ELSE `watching, guarding and protecting property`

-- s 52(1)(g)(i): the course, "except where section 53 applies". s 53(2): the officer "may in writing exempt an applicant"
-- (and may make completion a condition). s 53(3): not "an applicant for a security officer's licence who has applied for an
-- endorsement under section 24 or 26."
GIVEN `the application` IS A `My application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`my training is done or excused` MEANS
       `Which training course must I complete` `the application` EQUALS `none is prescribed: monitoring duties only`
    OR `the application`'s `I have completed the prescribed training course`
    OR (     `the application`'s `the officer exempted me from the training course`
         AND (NOT `the application`'s `I am applying for a firearm endorsement`)
         AND (NOT `the application`'s `I am applying for a baton endorsement`))

DECLARE `Licence decision` IS ONE OF
    `the officer may issue the licence`
    `not issued: the application is not properly made`
    `not issued: identity not established`
    `not issued: I am under 18`
    `not issued: not of good character, or not fit and proper`
    `not issued: I am a prohibited person`
    `not issued: a disqualifying charge is pending, without extenuating circumstances`
    `not issued: the officer doubts I can comply with the conditions`
    `not issued: training not done`
    `not issued: examination not passed`
    `not issued: medical examination not passed`
    `not issued: contrary to the public interest, or another good reason`

-- s 52(1): "A licensing officer is not to issue a licence, other than a temporary licence, unless the officer is satisfied
-- -- (a) that there is sufficient evidence of the applicant's identity; and (b) in the case of ... a security officer's
-- licence ..., that the applicant has attained the age of 18 years; and (c) that the applicant is of good character and is
-- a fit and proper person to hold a licence; and (ca) that the applicant is not a prohibited person; and (cb) where there is
-- a charge pending in relation to the applicant for a disqualifying offence, that extenuating circumstances exist; and ...
-- (e) that during the licence period the applicant will be able to comply with any condition or restriction ...; and (g)
-- ... (i) ... satisfactorily completed any course of training prescribed ...; and (ii) passed any test or examination
-- prescribed ...; and (h) in the case of an application for a security officer's licence with an endorsement under section
-- 24, that the applicant has passed any prescribed medical examination; and (j) ... other requirements ... prescribed; and
-- (k) that there is no other good reason why the licence should not be issued." s 52A(2): "A licence can be issued only if
-- the licensing officer is satisfied that to issue the licence ... would not be contrary to the public interest."
-- Section 52 is written as a bar ("is not to issue ... unless"). It never says the officer must issue, so the best outcome
-- is that the officer MAY. The first unmet limb, in the order of s 52(1), is the answer.
@export Can I be issued a security officer's licence (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) ss 52, 52A, 53)?
GIVEN `the application` IS A `My application` @desc Your application for a security officer's licence
GIVETH A `Licence decision`
`Can I be issued a security officer's licence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application`'s `it is in the approved form, lodged as prescribed, with the fee`
            THEN `not issued: the application is not properly made`
        IF NOT `the application`'s `the officer accepts the evidence of my identity`
            THEN `not issued: identity not established`
        IF `age in completed years` (`the application`'s `my date of birth`) (`the application`'s `the date of the decision`)
               LESS THAN `the minimum age for a security officer's licence`
            THEN `not issued: I am under 18`
        IF NOT `the application`'s `the officer is satisfied I am of good character and fit and proper`
            THEN `not issued: not of good character, or not fit and proper`
        IF `Am I a prohibited person` (`the application`'s `my past matters`) (`the application`'s `the date of the decision`)
            THEN `not issued: I am a prohibited person`
        IF     `the application`'s `a charge for a disqualifying offence is pending against me`
           AND (NOT `the application`'s `the officer is satisfied extenuating circumstances exist`)
            THEN `not issued: a disqualifying charge is pending, without extenuating circumstances`
        IF NOT `the application`'s `the officer is satisfied I can comply with the licence conditions`
            THEN `not issued: the officer doubts I can comply with the conditions`
        IF NOT `my training is done or excused` `the application`
            THEN `not issued: training not done`
        IF NOT `the application`'s `I have passed the written examination`
            THEN `not issued: examination not passed`
        IF     `the application`'s `I am applying for a firearm endorsement`
           AND (NOT `the application`'s `I have passed the prescribed medical examination`)
            THEN `not issued: medical examination not passed`
        IF     (NOT `the application`'s `the officer is satisfied issuing it is not contrary to the public interest`)
            OR (NOT `the application`'s `the officer sees no other good reason to refuse`)
            THEN `not issued: contrary to the public interest, or another good reason`
        OTHERWISE `the officer may issue the licence`

-- s 57(1): "Where a licensing officer refuses to issue a licence the officer, no later than 28 days after the decision is
-- made, is to give written notice to the applicant setting out the decision and the reasons for the decision."
@export Was I given written reasons for refusing my licence in time (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 57(1))?
GIVEN `the date of the refusal` IS A DATE @desc The day the licensing officer decided to refuse
      `the date of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given the written notice with reasons
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I given reasons for the refusal in time` IF
    `days from` `the date of the refusal` `the date of the notice` AT MOST `the days after a refused issue for notice`

§§ `Sch 4 -- what it costs`

-- reg 54: "The fees set out in column 3 of Schedule 4 are prescribed". Schedule 4 (SL 2026/115), "Other licences,
-- endorsements and permits": issue of a licence (other than an agent's or temporary licence) "for 1 year or less" $405, "for
-- more than 1 year but not more than 3 years" $434; an additional licence $244; renewal "for 3 years or less" $272; a
-- temporary licence under s 42A $405; a s 24 or s 26 endorsement $240; a s 25 permit $284. "Additional fee if fingerprints
-- and palm prints are required under s. 48(1)(a) or (b)(i)" $135 (s 94(4)(b)). Agent's licence fees are not encoded.
DECLARE `Fee item` IS ONE OF
    `a new licence for 1 year or less`
    `a new licence for more than 1 year, up to 3 years`
    `an additional licence for a current licensee`
    `renewing a licence for 3 years or less`
    `a temporary licence for an interstate resident`
    `a firearm or baton endorsement`
    `a firearm permit for a special occasion`

@export What fee do I pay (Security and Related Activities (Control) Regulations 1997 reg 54, Sch 4)?
GIVEN `the item` IS A `Fee item` @desc What you are applying for
      `my fingerprints and palm prints are required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensing officer requires your fingerprints and palm prints for a licence or its renewal
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What fee do I pay` MEANS
    `the base fee` PLUS `the fingerprint fee`
    WHERE
        `the base fee` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the item`
            WHEN `a new licence for 1 year or less` THEN 405
            WHEN `a new licence for more than 1 year, up to 3 years` THEN 434
            WHEN `an additional licence for a current licensee` THEN 244
            WHEN `renewing a licence for 3 years or less` THEN 272
            WHEN `a temporary licence for an interstate resident` THEN 405
            WHEN `a firearm or baton endorsement` THEN 240
            WHEN `a firearm permit for a special occasion` THEN 284
        `the fingerprint fee` MEANS
            IF `my fingerprints and palm prints are required` THEN 135 ELSE 0

§§ `42A, 49, 55, 57, 60 -- how long it runs and renewing it`

-- s 60: "Subject to this Act, except for the first issue of a licence, a licence shall be issued or renewed -- (a) for a
-- period of 3 years, or such shorter period as is requested; or (b) for the duration of a special event or events, as is
-- specified in the licence." s 42A(2): a temporary licence "is to be granted for such period of time of not more than one
-- year as is specified in the licence; and (b) is not renewable."
-- The words "except for the first issue" leave the first term unfixed by s 60. Schedule 4 prices a new licence for "1 year
-- or less" or "more than 1 year but not more than 3 years", so 3 years is the most the fees contemplate (an inference).
DECLARE `Licence term` IS ONE OF
    `3 years`
    `the shorter period I asked for`
    `the special event or events named in the licence`
    `not fixed by s 60 for a first issue: up to 3 years under the fee scale`
    `up to 1 year, as the temporary licence states, and it cannot be renewed`

@export How long will my licence run (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) ss 42A, 60)?
GIVEN `it is a temporary licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a temporary licence for an interstate resident (s 42A)
      `it is the first issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this is the first time the licence is issued to you
      `it is for a special event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licence is for the duration of a special event or events
      `I asked for a period shorter than 3 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked for less than 3 years
GIVETH A `Licence term`
`How long will my licence run` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a temporary licence` THEN `up to 1 year, as the temporary licence states, and it cannot be renewed`
        IF `it is the first issue` THEN `not fixed by s 60 for a first issue: up to 3 years under the fee scale`
        IF `it is for a special event` THEN `the special event or events named in the licence`
        IF `I asked for a period shorter than 3 years` THEN `the shorter period I asked for`
        OTHERWISE `3 years`

-- s 49(3): "An application for the renewal of a licence is to be made no later than 28 days before the day on which the
-- licence is due to expire or at such later time as the licensing officer, having regard to section 57(2), allows."
-- Reg 19: by post, received by then, or in person.
@export Is my renewal application on time (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 49(3))?
GIVEN `the expiry date` IS A DATE @desc The day your licence is due to expire
      `the day the application is received` IS A DATE @desc The day the licensing officer receives your renewal application
      `the licensing officer allowed a later time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensing officer allowed you to apply later
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my renewal application on time` IF
       `days from` `the day the application is received` `the expiry date` AT LEAST `the days before expiry to apply for renewal`
    OR `the licensing officer allowed a later time`

-- s 55(1): the officer "is not to renew an applicant's licence -- (a) if in the officer's opinion there are sufficient
-- grounds -- (i) to make an allegation to the State Administrative Tribunal under section 67(1) ...; or (ii) for the
-- exercise of the power to revoke the licence under section 67A(1)(a) or 81(1); or (iii) for the exercise of the power to
-- suspend the licence under section 67A(2); or (b) if the officer is satisfied that the applicant is a prohibited person."
-- (2): despite (1)(a)(i), the officer may renew if the allegation would be under s 67(1a)(c), (d) or (e) (an endorsement
-- that could be cancelled, a code of conduct breach, a breach of the Act or a licence condition) and the officer thinks it
-- "appropriate ... in the circumstances of the particular case".
DECLARE `Ground against renewal` IS ONE OF
    `no ground`
    `a minor ground: an endorsement could be cancelled, or I breached the Act, a condition or a code of conduct`
    `another ground for an allegation to the Tribunal`
    `a ground to revoke or suspend my licence summarily`

DECLARE `Renewal decision` IS ONE OF
    `the officer may renew my licence`
    `not renewed: I am a prohibited person`
    `not renewed: there are grounds against me`

@export Can my licence be renewed (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 55)?
GIVEN `my past matters` IS A LIST OF `My past matter` @desc Every charge against you and what came of each
      `the date of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day the renewal is decided
      `the ground` IS A `Ground against renewal` @desc The ground, in the licensing officer's opinion, against renewing your licence
      `the officer thinks renewing is appropriate anyway` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensing officer thinks it appropriate to renew despite a minor ground
GIVETH A `Renewal decision`
`Can my licence be renewed` MEANS
    IF `Am I a prohibited person` `my past matters` `the date of the decision`
    THEN `not renewed: I am a prohibited person`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the ground`
         WHEN `no ground` THEN `the officer may renew my licence`
         WHEN `a minor ground: an endorsement could be cancelled, or I breached the Act, a condition or a code of conduct` THEN
             IF `the officer thinks renewing is appropriate anyway`
             THEN `the officer may renew my licence`
             ELSE `not renewed: there are grounds against me`
         OTHERWISE `not renewed: there are grounds against me`

-- s 57(2): "Where a licensing officer refuses to renew a licence the officer, no later than 14 days before the day on which
-- the licence is due to expire, is to give written notice to the applicant setting out the decision and the reasons".
@export Was I told in time that my licence will not be renewed (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 57(2))?
GIVEN `the expiry date` IS A DATE @desc The day your licence is due to expire
      `the date of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given written notice of the refusal and the reasons
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I told in time that my licence will not be renewed` IF
    `days from` `the date of the notice` `the expiry date` AT LEAST `the days before expiry for notice of a refused renewal`

§§ `61, 77, 77A, Sch 1 cl 7, 11B -- at work and afterwards`

-- Sch 1 Div 2 (conditions on every security officer's licence, reg 21(b); breach is an offence under s 64):
-- cl 11B(1): "A security officer must not perform any licensed activity unless the officer holds a current first aid
-- certificate." cl 7(1): a uniform "of a type approved by the Commissioner" at all times while performing a licensed
-- activity; (3): not for "(a) ... loss prevention activities in a retail store; or (b) ... escort duties if a licensing
-- officer is satisfied that the circumstances require" other clothes. cl 9(3): no "other weapon".
@export May I start my shift on these facts (Regulations Sch 1 Div 2 cl 7, 9(3), 11B)?
GIVEN `I hold a current first aid certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a current first aid certificate from an approved course
      `I am wearing an approved uniform` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are wearing a uniform of a type the Commissioner approved
      `I am doing retail loss prevention, or an escort the officer allowed out of uniform` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the uniform exception in cl 7(3) applies to you
      `I carry a weapon other than an authorised firearm or baton` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are carrying any other weapon
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I start my shift` IF
        `I hold a current first aid certificate`
    AND (`I am wearing an approved uniform` OR `I am doing retail loss prevention, or an escort the officer allowed out of uniform`)
    AND (NOT `I carry a weapon other than an authorised firearm or baton`)

-- s 61(2): a licensee issued an identity card "must, on request, immediately produce the card for inspection by -- (a) a
-- compliance officer or a police officer; or (b) any person for whom the licensee is performing services under the
-- licence, and must have the card in his or her possession". Penalty $200; (3) reasonable excuse is a defence.
DECLARE `Who is asking` IS ONE OF
    `a police officer`
    `a compliance officer`
    `the client I am guarding for`
    `a member of the public`

@export Must I show my identity card to this person (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 61(2))?
GIVEN `who is asking` IS A `Who is asking` @desc Who asked to see your card
      `I was issued an identity card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a licensing officer issued you an identity card
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I show my identity card` IF
        `I was issued an identity card`
    AND (CONSIDER `who is asking`
         WHEN `a member of the public` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

-- s 77A(1): "A licensee must give to a licensing officer written notice within 7 days after -- (a) being charged with a
-- disqualifying offence; or (b) there has been a finding of guilt in relation to an offence committed by the licensee".
-- Note (b) is any offence, not only a disqualifying one. s 77(2): a change of residence, "not later than 14 days after".
DECLARE `What happened to me` IS ONE OF
    `I was charged with a disqualifying offence`
    `I was charged with an offence that is not disqualifying`
    `a court found me guilty of any offence`
    `I moved house`

DECLARE `Notice duty` IS ONE OF
    `tell a licensing officer in writing within 7 days`
    `tell a licensing officer within 14 days`
    `no duty to tell under this Act`

@export Must I tell the licensing officer, and by when (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) ss 77(2), 77A)?
GIVEN `the event` IS A `What happened to me` @desc What happened
GIVETH A `Notice duty`
`Must I tell the licensing officer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the event`
    WHEN `I was charged with a disqualifying offence` THEN `tell a licensing officer in writing within 7 days`
    WHEN `a court found me guilty of any offence` THEN `tell a licensing officer in writing within 7 days`
    WHEN `I moved house` THEN `tell a licensing officer within 14 days`
    OTHERWISE `no duty to tell under this Act`

@export Did I tell the licensing officer in time (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) ss 77(2), 77A)?
GIVEN `the event` IS A `What happened to me` @desc What happened
      `the date it happened` IS A DATE @desc The day of the charge, finding or move
      `the date I told them` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the licensing officer notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I tell the licensing officer in time` IF
    CONSIDER `Must I tell the licensing officer` `the event`
    WHEN `tell a licensing officer in writing within 7 days` THEN
        `days from` `the date it happened` `the date I told them` AT MOST `the days to report a charge or a finding of guilt`
    WHEN `tell a licensing officer within 14 days` THEN
        `days from` `the date it happened` `the date I told them` AT MOST `the days to report a new home address`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `67A, 69(1a), 79B, 80, 81 -- what can happen to my licence`

-- s 67A(1): if the Commissioner "(a) is of the opinion that the safety or welfare of members of the public is or may be at
-- risk ...; or (b) is satisfied that a licensee is a prohibited person", the Commissioner "must give ... written notice of
-- the revocation of the licence or, if paragraph (b) is applicable, of every licence", and they "are revoked when the notice
-- is received". For (a), the matter goes to the State Administrative Tribunal within 14 days (67A(1)(d), (4)).
-- (2)(c): "there is a charge pending ... for a disqualifying offence and ... no extenuating circumstances exist" -- every
-- licence is suspended on receipt, with referral to the Tribunal within 14 days. s 69(1a): a court sentencing for a
-- disqualifying offence may not itself revoke the licence under s 69(1); s 67A does the work.
DECLARE `What the Commissioner concludes` IS ONE OF
    `I have become a prohibited person`
    `the public is or may be at risk from my licence`
    `a disqualifying charge is pending and there are no extenuating circumstances`
    `nothing against me`

DECLARE `What happens to my licence` IS ONE OF
    `every licence I hold is revoked when I receive the notice`
    `my licence is revoked when I receive the notice, and the matter goes to the Tribunal within 14 days`
    `every licence I hold is suspended when I receive the notice, and the matter goes to the Tribunal within 14 days`
    `nothing under s 67A`

@export What happens to my licence (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 67A)?
GIVEN `the conclusion` IS A `What the Commissioner concludes` @desc What the Commissioner has concluded about you
GIVETH A `What happens to my licence`
`What happens to my licence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the conclusion`
    WHEN `I have become a prohibited person` THEN `every licence I hold is revoked when I receive the notice`
    WHEN `the public is or may be at risk from my licence` THEN `my licence is revoked when I receive the notice, and the matter goes to the Tribunal within 14 days`
    WHEN `a disqualifying charge is pending and there are no extenuating circumstances` THEN `every licence I hold is suspended when I receive the notice, and the matter goes to the Tribunal within 14 days`
    OTHERWISE `nothing under s 67A`

-- s 79B: for Part 9, "licensee means the holder of -- (a) a crowd controller's licence; or (b) a security officer's licence
-- with an endorsement under section 24 or 26; or (c) a security officer's licence and a permit under section 25." s 80(1):
-- "The Commissioner may at any time direct a licensee to attend at a place and there give a sample of his or her blood or
-- urine". s 81(1): failing to comply, or a noncomplying sample, may lead to revocation (after 21 days to respond, s 81(2a)).
-- An unendorsed security officer is outside Part 9.
@export Can the Commissioner direct me to give a blood or urine sample (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) ss 79B, 80)?
GIVEN `I hold a crowd controller's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a crowd controller's licence
      `my security officer's licence has a firearm or baton endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your licence is endorsed under s 24 or s 26
      `I hold a firearm permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a s 25 permit with your security officer's licence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commissioner direct me to give a sample` IF
    `I hold a crowd controller's licence` OR `my security officer's licence has a firearm or baton endorsement` OR `I hold a firearm permit`

§§ `72 -- review`

-- s 72(1): "Any person aggrieved by a reviewable decision of a licensing officer may apply to State Administrative Tribunal
-- for a review". (2): a reviewable decision is one "(a) to refuse to issue or renew a licence or refuse to grant an
-- endorsement under section 24 or 26; or (b) as to the period for which a licence is issued or renewed; or (c) as to a
-- condition or restriction ...; or (ca) to refuse to issue a permit under section 25; or (cb) as to the period for which a
-- permit ... is issued; or (d) to revoke or suspend a licence; or (e) to cancel an endorsement".
DECLARE `Licensing decision` IS ONE OF
    `refusing to issue or renew my licence`
    `refusing an endorsement`
    `the period my licence was issued or renewed for`
    `a condition or restriction on my licence`
    `refusing a firearm permit`
    `revoking or suspending my licence`
    `cancelling an endorsement`
    `refusing to exempt me from training`

@export May I ask the State Administrative Tribunal to review this decision (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 72)?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Licensing decision` @desc The licensing officer's decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask the Tribunal to review this decision` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `refusing to exempt me from training` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `penalties, s 88A, Sch 5`

-- The fines a court may impose, as stated in each section: s 16 "$15 000"; s 64 (a licence condition) "$15 000"; s 51
-- (false information) "$15 000"; s 77(2), s 77A, s 75 "$2 000"; s 61(2) "$200".
-- s 88A(1): an infringement notice may be given for "a prescribed offence"; Sch 5 Div 1 modified penalties: item 2 (s 16)
-- $500, item 21 (s 64) $500, item 24 (s 75) $400, item 27 (s 77(2)) $400, item 28 (s 77A(1)) $400. s 61 and s 51 are not
-- prescribed. s 88A(5): a modified penalty may not exceed 20% of the maximum.
DECLARE `My offence` IS ONE OF
    `working as a security officer without a licence`
    `breaching a condition of my licence`
    `giving false or misleading information in my application`
    `not producing my licence when asked`
    `not reporting a new home address`
    `not reporting a charge or a finding of guilt`
    `not producing my identity card`

@export What is the most a court can fine me (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) ss 16, 51, 61, 64, 75, 77, 77A)?
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `My offence` @desc The offence you are said to have committed
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most a court can fine me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `working as a security officer without a licence` THEN 15000
    WHEN `breaching a condition of my licence` THEN 15000
    WHEN `giving false or misleading information in my application` THEN 15000
    WHEN `not producing my identity card` THEN 200
    OTHERWISE 2000

@export Can I be given an infringement notice for this offence (Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) s 88A; Regulations Sch 5)?
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `My offence` @desc The offence you are said to have committed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be given an infringement notice` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `giving false or misleading information in my application` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `not producing my identity card` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- The modified penalty for an offence that can be dealt with by infringement notice (Sch 5 Div 1); 0 where none is
-- prescribed (s 51, s 61), in which case the offence goes to court.
@export What is the modified penalty on an infringement notice (Regulations Sch 5 Div 1)?
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `My offence` @desc The offence you are said to have committed
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the modified penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `working as a security officer without a licence` THEN 500
    WHEN `breaching a condition of my licence` THEN 500
    WHEN `giving false or misleading information in my application` THEN 0
    WHEN `not producing my identity card` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 400
